<pre><code>valid = true;
$("#studentForm input.mustEnter, #studentForm input.mustCheck").each(function() {
    if( ($(this).hasClass('mustEnter') && $(this).val() != false ) 
     || ($(this).hasClass('mustCheck') && $(this).is(':checked')) ) {
        $(this).parent().removeClass("errorHighlight");
    } else { 
        $(this).parent().addClass('errorHighlight');
        valid = false;
    }
});
</code></pre>

With the updated code, <code>$(this).is(':checked')</code> is used to check if at least one option is checked for radio buttons and checkboxes. This should correctly highlight the error field if any mandatory field is not filled or checked.

